MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Client-only change, no protocol/server modifications. One /api/list +
local scan. Verdict is hash-only (no mtime fast path) so diff never
contradicts push/push's skip decision; statuses are directional-neutral:
modified / local-only / server-only.

Return value in three layers: exit codes 0 (in sync) / 1 (differs) /
2 (error); --json ({inSync, files[{path,status,local,server}], summary},
path-sorted) with pure-JSON stdout; git-status-style human output.
Server dir missing is a fact (local-only), not an error, unlike pull.

Tests: 6 unit (hash-only, three statuses, win32 paths, sort order) +
4 integration (exit 0 after pull, exit 1 with all three statuses,
pattern scope, exit 2 unconfigured) — 121 total pass. --content
single-file line diff is planned next.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
